WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.333
From a craving to a kitchen commitment.

2
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:12.600
One fictional restaurant. Two service windows to coordinate.

3
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:25.300
The exact synthetic request Muse received is preserved.

4
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:38.467
Muse retrieved dated facts and used the quantity-checking tool.

5
00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:45.967
The extracted draft preserves the counts and both service windows.

6
00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:56.767
Adopt the draft. Keep the 12-versus-13 conflict visible.

7
00:00:56.767 --> 00:01:10.800
After an authored guest clarification, the current-menu quote is $213.

8
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:23.233
Review price, timing and capacity before approving version 3.

9
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:34.100
Two simulated receipts acknowledge the exact approved version.

10
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:47.200
One more pizza creates version 4. Earlier receipts stay historical.

11
00:01:47.200 --> 00:02:01.967
“Pickup only today” keeps its restaurant, date and history.

12
00:02:01.967 --> 00:02:10.733
The next delivery request stops for pickup confirmation.

13
00:02:10.733 --> 00:02:23.567
A separate recorded review found the rule—with disclosed limits.

14
00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:30.000
Missing fulfillment stays visible. Draft adoption remains disabled.

15
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.400
Action Shift by Never86’d. From craving to kitchen.
